WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.590
(alarm sounding in distance)

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:02.800
- [Voiceover] Warm out.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.538
- [Voiceover] How long has it been?

00:00:03.538 --> 00:00:04.970
- [Voiceover] Alright, good job guys.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.143
Good job.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:07.710
But I'm gonna have to
ask you all one last time

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.742
respect the drill, okay?

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:11.750
Fire safety is no laughing matter.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.260
I can tell you all a
pretty gruesome story.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.246
- Charlie, do we have to do this now?

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:15.082
I have so much work to do.

00:00:15.082 --> 00:00:16.788
- You make us do this
dumb drill every month,

00:00:16.788 --> 00:00:19.029
and every month there's no fire.

00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:20.806
- Well hopefully a fire
doesn't break out, okay?

00:00:20.806 --> 00:00:24.022
That's why we have to respect the drill.

00:00:24.022 --> 00:00:26.374
- Harper, what are you doing?

00:00:26.374 --> 00:00:27.318
- It's a long island.

00:00:27.318 --> 00:00:28.944
I make one every morning, just in case.

00:00:28.944 --> 00:00:29.641
- Smart.

00:00:29.641 --> 00:00:30.905
- It's the middle of the work day.

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:31.823
- We're outside.

00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:32.589
This is international waters.

00:00:32.589 --> 00:00:33.982
Your rules don't apply here.

00:00:33.982 --> 00:00:34.865
- Is that true?

00:00:34.865 --> 00:00:35.747
- [Harper] Mm-hm.

00:00:35.747 --> 00:00:37.780
- Charlie, I really need
to get back to work.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.427
- Kalen, put your shirt back on.

00:00:39.427 --> 00:00:40.315
Harper, stop drinking.

00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:42.909
- Guys, please respect the drill, okay?

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:43.885
Alright, that's illegal.

00:00:43.885 --> 00:00:45.580
Anna, Anna come back here.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:46.683
You need to imagine that this building

00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:49.293
is a flaming tinderbox of death.

00:00:50.203 --> 00:00:51.312
Great, now I have to start...

00:00:51.312 --> 00:00:52.952
I have to start the timer all over.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:53.950
- [Kalen] So in international waters

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.564
I can do whatever I want?

00:00:55.564 --> 00:00:56.447
- Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:00:56.447 --> 00:00:58.606
You're thinking of diplomatic immunity.

00:00:58.606 --> 00:01:00.522
- Right, like in "Lethal Weapon 2."

00:01:00.522 --> 00:01:01.310
- [Harper] Yeah.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:03.424
- How are we only getting worse, guys?

00:01:03.424 --> 00:01:06.636
- Okay, so you're saying if
I die in international waters

00:01:06.636 --> 00:01:08.621
I die in real life?

00:01:08.621 --> 00:01:09.832
- No, I would never say that.

00:01:09.832 --> 00:01:10.911
That makes no sense.

00:01:10.911 --> 00:01:12.061
- Okay, if we don't get wi-fi out here,

00:01:12.061 --> 00:01:14.523
I'm going back inside,
imaginary fire or no.

00:01:14.523 --> 00:01:16.101
- Guys, please.

00:01:16.101 --> 00:01:17.704
Respect the drill.

00:01:17.704 --> 00:01:18.481
- Can we wrap this up?

00:01:18.481 --> 00:01:19.921
Kalen thinks he's on vacation.

00:01:19.921 --> 00:01:21.650
I'm afraid he's gonna take his pants off.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.090
- That's it.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.272
No, no, you guys think
this is all fun and games,

00:01:25.272 --> 00:01:26.492
don't you, huh?

00:01:26.492 --> 00:01:29.451
Well, well if you're not gonna respect me,

00:01:29.451 --> 00:01:31.979
then respect the drill.

00:01:32.787 --> 00:01:35.431
- Wait, you think we don't respect you?

00:01:35.431 --> 00:01:36.722
- Is that what this is about?

00:01:37.262 --> 00:01:38.183
- I don't know.

00:01:38.183 --> 00:01:39.123
I just...

00:01:39.123 --> 00:01:40.644
Sometimes I feel like you guys don't care

00:01:40.644 --> 00:01:41.932
about what I do here.

00:01:41.932 --> 00:01:43.429
- We're sorry, Charlie.

00:01:43.429 --> 00:01:44.578
- Yeah.

00:01:44.578 --> 00:01:46.663
We didn't know how
important this was to you.

00:01:47.363 --> 00:01:49.629
We really appreciate
you looking out for us.

00:01:49.629 --> 00:01:51.905
- Yeah, we um, we respect you.

00:01:51.905 --> 00:01:54.059
- You're very important to me,

00:01:56.061 --> 00:01:58.327
as an employee.

00:01:58.327 --> 00:02:00.426
- Well thanks, guys.

00:02:00.426 --> 00:02:01.703
Huh.

00:02:01.703 --> 00:02:03.282
I guess I can get a little too worked up

00:02:03.282 --> 00:02:05.952
about a silly fire drill, huh?

00:02:07.032 --> 00:02:08.379
Well, you guys know to leave the building

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:09.841
when the alarm goes off, right?

00:02:09.841 --> 00:02:10.956
- Yes.

00:02:10.956 --> 00:02:12.117
- Obviously.

00:02:12.117 --> 00:02:15.908
(keyboard clicking)
(louder alarm)

00:02:24.296 --> 00:02:25.723
- I guess I just thought it was like,

00:02:25.723 --> 00:02:26.675
cause there are no laws,

00:02:26.675 --> 00:02:30.215
that men of like physics and biology,

00:02:30.215 --> 00:02:31.156
and math,

00:02:31.156 --> 00:02:33.778
like you could just add
whatever numbers you wanted,

00:02:34.548 --> 00:02:36.287
and it just wouldn't matter.

00:02:36.287 --> 00:02:37.685
- [Harper] No.

